        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d7fcfc74-81a9-57e0-b806-6e1fd8c7b657",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alan Young, Charles Dickens\n- Characters: Scrooge McDuck, Ebenezer Scrooge\n- Works: The Alan Young Show, Mickey's Christmas Carol, A Christmas Carol\n- Organizations: Disney, TV Guide, Academy Awards, Emmy Awards\n\nFacts:\n- Alan Young was born Angus Young on November 19, 1919, and he was a British-born Canadian-American actor, voice actor, comedian, and radio and television host.\n- During the 1940s and 1950s, Alan Young starred in his own variety and comedy sketch program, The Alan Young Show, on radio and television.\n- In 1951, the television version of The Alan Young Show won Alan Young two Emmy Awards.\n- TV Guide called Alan Young \"The Charlie Chaplin of Television.\"\n- In 1983, Alan Young first voiced Disney's Scrooge McDuck in Mickey's Christmas Carol.\n- Mickey's Christmas Carol is an adaptation of Charles Dickens' A Christmas Carol.\n- Mickey's Christmas Carol stars Scrooge McDuck as Ebenezer Scrooge.\n- Mickey's Christmas Carol was nominated for an Academy Award.\n- Alan Young voiced Scrooge McDuck in films, television series, and video games for more than thirty years until his death on May 19, 2016.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "8879302b-abd3-5141-9ea4-485216179ca6",
